id: pm-58yzil
title: Enable explicit successful-command Sentry tracing without eager startup
description: "A fresh24h Sentry trace query returned zero rows after a successful read with SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=1. Successful-command span helpers require an already-initialized client, while current CLI initialization is lazy on error-reporting paths. Preserve that completed startup optimization and add an explicit, bounded tracing opt-in that can initialize and flush successful command spans without manufacturing errors."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: feature,observability,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-12T19:21:47.566Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T13:35:14.821Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T13:35:13.935Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T13:35:13.935Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Prove an independent successful-command opt-in control before and after; honor consent opt-outs and Vitest isolation; sanitize span context; preserve default cold-start and import budgets; verify one recent explicitly sampled trace through the authenticated Sentry API, distinguishing ingestion unavailability from source behavior."
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Expose explicit tracing permission and cancellation, preserve command outcomes on unavailable completion consent, return false for initialization failures without retries, and publish the Sentry module only after successful initialization"
expected_result: Optional diagnostics never block actions or expose a partial client; concurrent callers receive no permission after a failed initialization
actual_result: "Loader, initializer, concurrent partial-client and completion-read controls fail before their corrections and pass afterward;100 linked Sentry checks and128 focused checks pass; direct unsuppressed lint, typecheck and final9-package npm/Bun/npx/bunx acceptance pass; exact revised hosted coverage and bot review remain required"
